<p>Lebanon&#x27;s health ministry said Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon killed 13 people, including four women and a child, with deaths reported in Habboush, Zrariyeh and Ain Baal despite a ceasefire that took effect on April 17. Lebanese state media also reported strikes across southern villages, including Choukin and areas near Tyre, with casualty figures differing across reports of separate incidents. The Israel Defense Forces said it struck Hezbollah-linked sites in southern Lebanon, including about 70 military infrastructure sites and about 50 other infrastructure facilities, and said it would act against Hezbollah violations of the ceasefire. The army issued evacuation warnings to residents of nine southern villages before some strikes, while Hezbollah said it targeted Israeli soldiers with drones or rockets, according to several accounts. Lebanon&#x27;s National News Agency reported Israeli strikes and artillery fire in additional locations in the south, while local and regional reports said Israeli forces also carried out demolitions in areas near the border. In Yaroun, the superior general of the Basilian Salvatorian Sisters told The Associated Press that parts of an empty Catholic convent compound had been destroyed.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/tS92Qk53r2d9tY_OS7M499lTXsVf0T_gw5ndg52e5mNs36I19G-0TwJ59mGGL0ucWpQQ57hqup0GuBOj9gKyI0Byz1C-QhfJn5svU0gcJRBp-1e_lHbJAbRwL6PLBvslHYPmwZs1uFnnn4T_wndm2f9ZLdap6b_64y0K9azp8UU3gkxuW3ckd1FPYNXG7Th7pakn_DH9agSznaNJxrbv877oRMoX8GoTGC225kAD2AjWU2vmoE8vSG92e4yPYsWLXX31C8N_VvQiLlXD2g' alt='Scene from southern Lebanon after Israeli strikes, as used by The National in its report on strikes across the south.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Choukin official injured: Sky News Arabia, citing Lebanon&#x27;s NNA, said a strike on Choukin killed two people and wounded others, including Mayor Hussein Ali Ahmad.</li><li>Habboush sequence: The NNA reported that Israeli warplanes launched heavy strikes less than an hour after the evacuation warning, while an AFP photographer saw smoke after the raids, The Express Tribune reported.</li></ul><blockquote>What we heard is that it was destroyed with bulldozers - Gladys Sabbagh</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israel Defense Forces: The military said rockets fired toward its soldiers in southern Lebanon landed in open areas, and said its operations targeted Hezbollah operatives. (<a href='https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/defense-news/article-894870'>The Jerusalem Post</a>)</li><li>Lebanon&#x27;s health ministry: Beyond the fatalities, the ministry said the strikes also wounded 21 people in Habboush, four in Zrariyeh and seven in Ain Baal. (<a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2606101/lebanon-says-13-killed-in-israeli-strikes-in-south'>The Express Tribune</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: The group said it targeted Israeli soldiers in the al-Qantara area. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/israeli-airstrikes-hit-southern-lebanon-despite-ceasefire-549634/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li><li>Basilian Salvatorian Sisters: Gladys Sabbagh said she lacked further details about the damaged Yaroun compound because the village&#x27;s residents had been displaced. (<a href='http://www.asiaone.com/asia/israeli-airstrikes-kill-7-southern-lebanon-catholic-convent-bulldozed'>AsiaOne</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/05/02/at-least-seven-killed-in-lebanon-as-israeli-raids-continue-despite-ceasefire'>Seven killed in southern Lebanon amid Israeli airstrikes and ceasefire tensions</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/5/2/devastation-of-southern-lebanon-continues-under'>Devastation of Southern Lebanon continues under ‘ceasefire’</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cd7pn0zywggo'>Thirteen killed in Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon, health ministry says</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/iran-submits-14-poi